def solve():
    # Read N from stdin
    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()
    if not input_data:
        return
    n = int(input_data[0])
    
    # The problem asks for the sum of f(P) over all permutations P of (1, 2, ..., N).
    # f(P) is formed by concatenating the decimal representations of elements in P.
    # Let s_i be the string representation of integer i.
    # Let L_i be the length of s_i.
    # f(P) = s_{p1} + s_{p2} + ... + s_{pN}
    # This is equivalent to:
    # f(P) = \sum_{i=1}^N (value of s_{pi}) * 10^{\sum_{j=i+1}^N L_{pj}}
    
    # Let S = \sum_{i=1}^N L_i be the total length of all strings.
    # For a fixed i \in {1, ..., N}, it appears at position k \in {1, ..., N}
    # in (N-1)! permutations.
    # When i is at position k, its contribution to the sum is:
    # (value of s_i) * 10^{\sum_{j=k+1}^N L_{pj}}
    
    # Let's simplify. The total sum is \sum_{P} \sum_{k=1}^N (value of s_{pk}) * 10^{\sum_{j=k+1}^N L_{pj}}
    # Swap the summations: \sum_{i=1}^N (value of s_i) * \sum_{P} 10^{\sum_{j=k+1}^N L_{pj}}
    # where k is the position of i in permutation P.
    
    # Let's fix i and its position k. The remaining N-1 elements are distributed
    # in the remaining N-1 positions.
    # The sum of 10^{\sum_{j=k+1}^N L_{pj}} over all permutations of the remaining N-1 elements
    # is equivalent to:
    # (N-1)! * \sum_{subset \subset \{1..N\} \setminus \{i\}, |subset| = N-k} (average value of 10^{\sum_{j \in subset} L_j})
    
    # This looks like a dynamic programming problem or a generating functions problem.
    # Let x_j = 10^{L_j}. We want to find the sum of products of these x_j.
    # Actually, the contribution of i at position k depends only on the set of elements
    # appearing after it.
    
    # Let's re-evaluate:
    # Total Sum = \sum_{i=1}^N (value of s_i) * \sum_{k=1}^N (N-1)! * \sum_{subset \subset \{1..N\} \setminus \{i\}, |subset| = N-k} 10^{\sum_{j \in subset} L_j}
    # Let \sum_{subset \subset \{1..N\} \setminus \{i\}, |subset| = m} 10^{\sum_{j \in subset} L_j} be denoted by G(i, m).
    # Total Sum = \sum_{i=1}^N (value of s_i) * \sum_{m=0}^{N-1} (N-1)! * G(i, m)
    
    # G(i, m) is the coefficient of x^m in the polynomial \prod_{j \neq i} (1 + 10^{L_j} x).
    # Let Q(x) = \prod_{j=1}^N (1 + 10^{L_j} x).
    # Then \prod_{j \neq i} (1 + 10^{L_j} x) = Q(x) / (1 + 10^{L_i} x).
    
    # The sum we need is \sum_{m=0}^{N-1} G(i, m).
    # This is the sum of coefficients of Q(x) / (1 + 10^{L_i} x) from x^0 to x^{N-
